# 2. Answer the following questions
a. What is the medically relevant insight from the article?
The study reveals that neuroblastoma may originate from distinct embryonic cell lineages, particularly Schwann cell 
precursors in the adrenal gland. This provides important insight into the developmental biology of neuroblastoma.

b. Which genomics technology/ technologies were used?
Single cell RNA sequencing analysis
Single-cell transcriptomic analysis
RNA velocity analysis

# 3. Further related research questions
a. List and explain at least three questions/ hypotheses you can think of that
extend the analysis presented in the paper.
1) Which genes regulate the transformation of Schwann cell precursors into sympathoblasts?
The study identifies developmental origins. Researchers coudld further investigate the upstream mechanisms controlling them. 
For example, researchers could examine genes involved in cell proliferation, differentiation and survival, and pssibly 
reveal potential therapeutic targets for neuroblastoma.

2) Do different developmental origins of neuroblastoma respond different to chemotherapy?
Neuroblastomas derived from different embryonic precursor populations might have different sensitivity to chemotheraphy or
possibly responds differently to medication.

3) Do sympathoblasts originating from different precursor cells have different risks of developing into neuroblastoma?
Different origins might have different gene expressions and different developmental paths. These might influence on the 
risk and prognosis of neuroblastoma.

